COMMAND NAME: gpmigrator

Upgrades an existing Greenplum Database 3.1.x.x system to 3.2.

*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

gpmigrator <old_GPHOME_path> <new_GPHOME_path> 
[-d <master_data_directory>] [-l <logfile_directory>] [-q]

gpmigrator --version | --help


*****************************************************
PREREQUISITES
*****************************************************

The following are required prior to running this upgrade utility:

* Make sure you are logged in to the master host as the Greenplum 
  Database superuser (gpadmin).

* Install the Greenplum Database 3.2.0.x binaries on all Greenplum hosts.

* Verify the integrity of your 3.1.x.x system catalogs using the 3.2 
  gpcheckcat utility (located in your 3.2 installation $GPHOME/bin/lib). 
  If problems are found, contact Greenplum customer support.

* Check for and recover any failed segments in your current Greenplum 
  Database system (gpstate, gprecoverseg).

* Rebuild all bitmap indexes in your database (REINDEX).

* Remove the standby master from your system configuration 
  (gpinitstandby -r).

* Run the 3.2 gpdetective utility (located in your 3.2 installation 
  $GPHOME/bin) on your running 3.1.x.x system.

* Backup your 3.1.x.x databases (gpcrondump or ZFS snapshots).

* Do a clean shutdown of your 3.1.x.x system (gpstop).

* Set $GPHOME to point to the new 3.2 installation location.

* Inform all database users of the upgrade and lockout time frame. 
  Once gpmigrator is running, users will not be allowed on the system 
  until the upgrade is complete.


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The gpmigrator utility upgrades an existing Greenplum Database 3.1.x.x 
system to 3.2. It can also be used to downgrade a 3.2 system back to 3.1. 
This utility updates the system catalog and internal version number, but 
not the actual software binaries.

During the migration process, all client connections to the master will 
be locked out. The migration utility locks all client access to the master, 
however it does not block direct utility mode access to the segments. To 
ensure a safe upgrade, make sure users are aware that any connections to 
a Greenplum segment are not safe during the upgrade timeframe.

gpmigrator is an interactive utility. It should not be run in the background.


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

<old_GPHOME_path>

Required. The absolute path to the current version of Greenplum Database 
software you want to migrate away from.


<new_GPHOME_path>

Required. The absolute path to the new version of Greenplum Database 
software you want to migrate to.


-d <master_data_directory>

Optional. The current master host data directory. If not specified, 
the value set for $MASTER_DATA_DIRECTORY will be used.


-l <logfile_directory>

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/gpAdminLogs.


-q (quiet mode)

Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the screen, 
but is still written to the log file.


--help

Displays the online help.


--version

Displays the version of this utility. 


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

First make sure you are using the 3.2 version of the Greenplum utilities:

export GPHOME=/usr/local/greenplum-db-3.2.0.0


Upgrade to version 3.2 from version 3.1.1.9:

gpmigrator /usr/local/greenplum-db-3.1.1.9 /usr/local/greenplum-db-3.2.0.0


